('/en/escalas-de-enfermagem/centro-cirurgico/index.html', 'en', 'secao', 'Surgical Center Scales: ASA, ELPO, Aldrete | Perioperative Nursing', 'Complete guide to surgical center scales: ASA for anesthetic risk, ELPO for positioning injury, Aldrete for post-anesthetic recovery. Interactive calculators.', 'Home
Nursing Scales
Surgical Center
SURGICAL CENTER
Surgical Center Scales
Instruments for preoperative assessment, intraoperative safety, and post-anesthetic recovery.
Quick Navigation
Introduction When to Use Comparison Flowchart Scales Related FAQ References
Introduction to Perioperative Scales
O perioperative comprises three distinct phases — preoperative, intraoperative, and postoperative — each with specific assessment needs. The perioperative nursing uses validated scales to systematize the assessment of surgical risk, prevention of adverse events, and safe discharge from the Post-Anesthesia Care Unit (PACU).
A ASA Classification (American Society of Anesthesiologists), created in 1941 and regularly revised, is the universal system for assessing preoperative physical status. It classifies the patient into 6 categories (ASA I to VI) based on the presence and severity of systemic diseases, and is an independent predictor of perioperative morbidity and mortality. ASA should be determined by the anesthesiologist during the pre-anesthetic consultation and recorded in the medical record and the safe surgery checklist.
In the intraoperative period, the ELPO assesses the risk of injuries from surgical positioning. In the PACU, the Aldrete and Kroulik Index is the gold standard for assessing post-anesthetic recovery and determining eligibility for discharge from the PACU. It assesses 5 parameters: motor activity, respiration, circulation, consciousness, and O2 saturation. Aldrete ≥ 9 indicates discharge conditions.
When to Use Each Scale
Perioperative Phase Scale Objective
Preoperative (consultation) ASA Assess physical status and anesthetic-surgical risk.
Preoperative (positioning) ELPO Assess risk of injury from surgical positioning.
Intraoperative ELPO Monitor and prevent pressure injuries intraoperatively.
PACU (admission and discharge) Aldrete Assess post-anesthetic recovery. ≥ 9 = discharge.
Safe Surgery Checklist WHO 3 stages: before induction, before incision, before closure.
Comparison between the Scales
Escala What it Assesses Range When
ASA Preoperative physical status (I to VI) I-VI Preoperative
ELPO Risk of pressure injury from positioning (7 items) 7-35 Pre and intraoperative
Aldrete Anesthetic recovery (5 parameters) 0-10 PACU (admission and discharge)
Perioperative Flowchart
Preoperative
↓
ASA (physical status) + ELPO (pressure injury risk)
↓
Transoperatório
↓
Safe Surgery Checklist (WHO) + ELPO (monitoring)
↓
PACU (admission)
↓
Aldrete (serial assessment every 15 min)
↓
Aldrete ≥ 9? Discharge from PACU
