W ↓ / I → I0 I1 I2 I3
W0 VL VL L M
W1 VL L L M
W2 L L M H
W3 M M H H
For fI = 2 (Moderate infection)
W ↓ / I → I0 I1 I2 I3
W0 L L L M
W1 L L M H
W2 M M M H
W3 M H H H
For fI = 3 (Severe infection + SIRS)
W ↓ / I → I0 I1 I2 I3
W0 M M M H
W1 M M M H
W2 M M H H
W3 H H H H
Legend: VL = Very Low L = Low M = Moderate H = High | Source: Adapted from MILLS et al. (2014, p. 228, Table IV).
5. Estimation of the Need/Benefit of Revascularization
The second matrix proposed by the SVS expert panel estimates the degree of need and the expected benefit of revascularization for each WIfI combination, assuming that the infection is controlled (MILLS et al., 2014, p. 229). This is Table V from the original article:
For fI = 0 (No infection)
