LANSS Scale
Leeds Assessment of Neuropathic Symptoms and Signs
The LANSS Scale (Leeds Assessment of Neuropathic Symptoms and Signs) is
a screening tool to identify pain with a neuropathic component.
The scale assesses patient symptoms and clinical signs examined by the
professional, resulting in a score that indicates the probability of
neuropathic pain. A total score of 12 or
more suggests a high probability of pain with a neuropathic
component.
Year of Creation: 2001
Authors: Dr. Linda B. Bennett and collaborators.
