NIPS Scale
Neonatal Infant Pain Scale: Pain Assessment in Newborns.
The NIPS (Neonatal Infant Pain Scale) is a tool for assessing pain in newborns and preterm infants. For each of the six parameters, select the option that best describes the newborn. A total score of 4 or more
indicates the presence of pain, requiring analgesic intervention.
Year of Creation: 1993
Authors: Lawrence et al.
Area of Use: Neonatal intensive care unit (NICU) and rooming-in.
Who uses it?: Neonatologists, pediatricians, and neonatal nurses.
