('/en/painad.html', 'en', 'secao', 'PAINAD Scale: Pain Assessment in Advanced Dementia - Nursing Calculators', 'Calculate the PAINAD Scale to assess pain in elderly patients with advanced dementia, focusing on non-verbal signs. Essential tool for palliative care.', 'Home
Pain Scales
PAINAD Scale
Geriatric / Palliative Assessment
PAINAD Scale
Pain Assessment in Advanced Dementia.
The PAINAD scale assesses pain in patients with advanced dementia who cannot verbalize
their discomfort. Through 5 behavioral domains (breathing, vocalization, facial expression,
body language, and consolability), it is possible to determine the need for intervention.
A total score of 4 or more indicates the presence of significant pain.
Year of Creation: 2003
Authors: Warden, Hurley, and Volicer.
Area of Use: Palliative Care, Geriatrics, Long-Term Care Facilities.
Who uses it?: Nurses, physicians, and multidisciplinary team.
