Risk Interpretation
Very High Risk (≥ 20 points)
Maximum risk. Requires aggressive prevention protocol: special mattresses (e.g., dynamic air), repositioning every 2h strictly and continuous reassessment.
High Risk (15 to 19 points)
High risk of developing PI. Implement advanced pressure relief measures, intense hydration, and nutritional control.
At Risk (10 to 14 points)
Patient presents active risk factors. Initiate basic prevention protocol, skin inspection, and standard position change.
Low Risk ( Minimal risk. Maintain routine hygiene, comfort care, and periodic reassessment.', 'publicado'),
